Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.35,0:00:03.84,Main,,0,0,0,,The value of intelligence is not just about\Ndoing calculations.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.88,0:00:06.50,Main,,0,0,0,,Learning, remembering, changing through\Nexperience,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.50,0:00:08.76,Main,,0,0,0,,and using what has been learned also\Nmatter.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.80,0:00:14.02,Main,,0,0,0,,DEE investigates these capabilities through\Na three-dimensional computational universe.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.06,0:00:19.26,Main,,0,0,0,,We will explore mechanisms that its\Nresearch has already put into operation.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.35,0:00:23.50,Main,,0,0,0,,In a trained neural network, learning can\Ninvolve
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.50,0:00:26.20,Main,,0,0,0,,adjusting the strength of its connections.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.24,0:00:31.54,Main,,0,0,0,,In DEE, the mechanism we will observe is\Ndifferent: elements move, meet,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.54,0:00:35.28,Main,,0,0,0,,and transform their organization under\Nfixed rules.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.33,0:00:40.67,Main,,0,0,0,,The computer executes those rules;\Nexperience changes the internal conditions
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.67,0:00:42.88,Main,,0,0,0,,that contribute to the response.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.35,0:00:48.28,Main,,0,0,0,,An experience leaves a relationship that\Ncan contribute again later.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.32,0:00:53.56,Main,,0,0,0,,In this test, two inputs meet and form a\Ntransformation relationship.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.60,0:00:58.66,Main,,0,0,0,,Later, a different signal arrives: when it\Nencounters what was learned, it changes.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.70,0:01:02.99,Main,,0,0,0,,The system thus uses a previous experience\Nwith a new input.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.03,0:01:09.59,Main,,0,0,0,,We call this learning: experience changes\Nhow subsequent inputs are processed.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.35,0:01:18.77,Main,,0,0,0,,Learning also includes revision.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.83,0:01:22.12,Main,,0,0,0,,First, a signal activates an acquired\Nrelationship.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.16,0:01:25.10,Main,,0,0,0,,Then a different experience is presented.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.23,0:01:29.87,Main,,0,0,0,,The same signal enters again, but now it\Nencounters a changed organization and
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.87,0:01:31.66,Main,,0,0,0,,produces a different response.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.70,0:01:35.50,Main,,0,0,0,,This is plasticity: changing an existing\Nrelationship.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.54,0:01:39.68,Main,,0,0,0,,Other associations can remain available\Nwhile this one is revised.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.72,0:01:43.05,Main,,0,0,0,,The difference lies in the system's\Nhistory;
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.05,0:01:45.92,Main,,0,0,0,,its fundamental rules remain the same.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.35,0:01:51.51,Main,,0,0,0,,Remembering means that this history becomes\Nuseful again.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.55,0:01:56.99,Main,,0,0,0,,DEE has shown relationships retained in\Ncarriers, differences between components,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.99,0:01:59.00,Main,,0,0,0,,and distributed organizations.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.04,0:02:03.48,Main,,0,0,0,,Some functions remain available after other\Nactivities and a waiting period.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.52,0:02:06.76,Main,,0,0,0,,And when a complete trajectory is saved and\Nreopened,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.76,0:02:09.21,Main,,0,0,0,,it can continue using what was acquired.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.35,0:02:13.41,Main,,0,0,0,,Learned relationships can also be combined.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.45,0:02:16.76,Main,,0,0,0,,Here, a query passes through two successive\Nencounters:
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.76,0:02:21.58,Main,,0,0,0,,the first relationship transforms the\Nsignal, and its result reaches the second.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.62,0:02:24.23,Main,,0,0,0,,The point is not the number thirty.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.27,0:02:27.60,Main,,0,0,0,,It is that two earlier experiences\Ncontribute
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.60,0:02:30.78,Main,,0,0,0,,to a processing chain within the DEE world.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.82,0:02:36.84,Main,,0,0,0,,Other experiments show that the order of\Ninteractions can also change the result.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.35,0:02:41.66,Main,,0,0,0,,Information can also travel between\Norganizations.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.71,0:02:44.22,Main,,0,0,0,,One participant receives an experience;
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.22,0:02:48.35,Main,,0,0,0,,a material message reaches another and\Nchanges a later response.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.40,0:02:53.16,Main,,0,0,0,,In other tests, a query makes it possible\Nto receive missing information and use it.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.20,0:02:55.72,Main,,0,0,0,,Communication therefore has a consequence:
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.72,0:02:59.37,Main,,0,0,0,,what happens in one place contributes to\Nwhat another can do.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.35,0:03:03.86,Main,,0,0,0,,Transfer means moving an acquired function\Nto another support,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.86,0:03:06.46,Main,,0,0,0,,or using an experience in a different\Ncontext.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.50,0:03:10.56,Main,,0,0,0,,DEE has demonstrated both possibilities in\Ndifferent experiments.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.60,0:03:12.95,Main,,0,0,0,,Communication routes have also been\Nprotected,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.95,0:03:15.91,Main,,0,0,0,,and useful functions recovered through\Nprepared resources.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.95,0:03:19.83,Main,,0,0,0,,The technological value lies in preserving\Nand reusing functions,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.83,0:03:21.38,Main,,0,0,0,,as well as acquiring them.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.35,0:03:26.11,Main,,0,0,0,,Using a memory depends on how it is\Naccessed.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.15,0:03:29.59,Main,,0,0,0,,Previously acquired content has been\Nrecovered by changing the access route,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.59,0:03:31.18,Main,,0,0,0,,without teaching the content again.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.22,0:03:36.89,Main,,0,0,0,,A real emission missed by the usual reader\Ncould be read at another moment and used.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.93,0:03:40.92,Main,,0,0,0,,We also confirmed that introducing a probe\Ncan change the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.96,0:03:46.90,Main,,0,0,0,,We therefore study information, access, and\Nthe effect of observation together.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.35,0:03:55.12,Main,,0,0,0,,Experience has also enabled anticipation of\Nan event before it occurs,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.12,0:03:56.76,Main,,0,0,0,,within tested sequences.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.80,0:03:59.43,Main,,0,0,0,,Other mechanisms link action, consequence,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.43,0:04:02.56,Main,,0,0,0,,and subsequent change through their own\Nevolution.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.60,0:04:05.63,Main,,0,0,0,,Time and order are part of the processing:
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.63,0:04:09.30,Main,,0,0,0,,what happened earlier changes what can\Nhappen next.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.35,0:04:13.39,Main,,0,0,0,,When a consequence returns to the system,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.39,0:04:16.94,Main,,0,0,0,,it can change a reference and a later\Nselection.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.98,0:04:22.59,Main,,0,0,0,,Adaptation experiments showed useful\Nactions that depended on this experience.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.63,0:04:27.30,Main,,0,0,0,,DEE outputs have also been connected to\Nenvironments and tools:
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.30,0:04:32.70,Main,,0,0,0,,an emission can produce an action, and its\Neffect can become a new input.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.35,0:04:38.14,Main,,0,0,0,,The landscape can receive and combine many\Ncontributions.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.18,0:04:42.14,Main,,0,0,0,,One experimental family integrated one\Nhundred and twenty-eight components,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.14,0:04:44.26,Main,,0,0,0,,testing the effect of changing each one.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.30,0:04:48.77,Main,,0,0,0,,In another trajectory, memory and\Ncomparison were used successively and
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.77,0:04:50.60,Main,,0,0,0,,during overlapping intervals.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.64,0:04:56.50,Main,,0,0,0,,We can thus study several activities in one\Nworld and observe how resources,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.50,0:04:59.44,Main,,0,0,0,,encounters, and timing influence them.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.35,0:05:03.86,Main,,0,0,0,,Words can also act as access signals.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.90,0:05:06.92,Main,,0,0,0,,A learned association can enable the use of\Na function,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.92,0:05:10.32,Main,,0,0,0,,and a revision can change which access is\Nactivated afterward.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.36,0:05:14.89,Main,,0,0,0,,In a recent test, revising what was learned\Nabout a signal changed which function
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.89,0:05:17.24,Main,,0,0,0,,was queried through a prepared connection.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.29,0:05:21.38,Main,,0,0,0,,The acquired experience had a concrete\Nfunctional consequence.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.35,0:05:25.02,Main,,0,0,0,,These mechanisms have also been used\Ntogether.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.06,0:05:29.07,Main,,0,0,0,,Some trajectories combine new associations,\Nearlier memories, queries,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.07,0:05:30.34,Main,,0,0,0,,and connected actions.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.38,0:05:33.77,Main,,0,0,0,,Others combine memory, comparison, and\Nnumerical operations,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.77,0:05:36.37,Main,,0,0,0,,using the result of one operation in the\Nnext.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.41,0:05:41.20,Main,,0,0,0,,Complete states can be saved and reopened\Nto continue the same history.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.35,0:05:45.98,Main,,0,0,0,,DEE brings together an engine, tools, and\Norganizations with history.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.02,0:05:48.04,Main,,0,0,0,,Its value lies in this diversity of\Nmechanisms
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.04,0:05:49.89,Main,,0,0,0,,and in how they can relate to one another.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.93,0:05:52.12,Main,,0,0,0,,This foundation opens development paths for
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.12,0:05:54.57,Main,,0,0,0,,adaptive systems and assistants with\Ncontinuity.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.61,0:05:59.30,Main,,0,0,0,,From Puebla, we seek collaboration to\Ndevelop and evaluate these possibilities.
